{"abstract":[{"text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"enum","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence14EntityCollapseO","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"title":"EntityCollapse"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Why-the-hook-takes-the-whole-collection","level":2,"text":"Why the hook takes the whole collection","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A per-ID resolver would only handle half the problem. Rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are one failure mode; the other is a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"singleton","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — an entity an app holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly one of, such as a settings record. Created independently on two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fresh installs, two singletons have ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"different","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" UUIDs, so nothing groups","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"them and no ID-keyed resolver can ever see the conflict. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"([E]) -> [E]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" hook covers both, plus general garbage collection, with one","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The determinism requirement","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-determinism-requirement"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver must be a pure function of ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"replicated content","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"persistentModelID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", never a local timestamp, never array position. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"device must compute the same survivor set from the same rows. A resolver","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that doesn’t reintroduces the mutual-tombstone loss the write path is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"designed to avoid: two devices pick different survivors, each tombstones the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other’s, and after sync "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"both","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" rows are gone.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It must also be idempotent — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse(collapse(rows))"},{"type":"text","text":" must keep the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"IDs as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse(rows)"},{"type":"text","text":". This is checked with an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assert"},{"type":"text","text":" in debug builds."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Collapse removes IDs, not rows","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Collapse-removes-IDs-not-rows"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A resolver’s output is read as "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the set of IDs that should exist and what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each should contain","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". An ID the resolver drops is deleted, including every","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"row carrying it. Several rows that share a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"surviving","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" ID are all updated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the survivor’s value, and none of them is deleted."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That asymmetry is deliberate, and it is the whole reason the singleton case"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the one this hook really solves. Deleting an ID is safe because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"replicated: every device independently computes the same set of doomed IDs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and issues the same deletions. Deleting one of several rows that share an ID","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" safe — nothing replicated distinguishes them, so two devices can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pick different physical rows to keep, each tombstones the other’s, and both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are lost.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Rows sharing an ID need no deletion anyway: writes already converge across","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every matching row and reads already collapse to one value per ID (see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"), so duplicates cost storage and nothing else.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"],"title":"Type Methods"}],"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitydb","abstract":[{"text":"A generic ","type":"text"},{"code":"@ModelActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that reads and writes any ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityDB","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityDB","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"EntityDB"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse","abstract":[{"text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"EntityCollapse"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence":{"kind":"symbol","title":"SwiduxPersistence","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","abstract":[]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse/byID(preferring:)":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byID","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"preferring","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ([","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"title":"byID(preferring:)","abstract":[{"text":"Collapses rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" down to one, keeping the winner of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"choose","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Rows with unique IDs pass through untouched.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse\/byid(preferring:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/PersistableModel":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistablemodel","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated SwiftData "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow for a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableEntity","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistableModel","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistableModel","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"PersistableModel"}}}